From 326962fa4d71700b8166f9338de66934f02ff9d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: n0madic <800462+n0madic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:16:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: FXAA on the picture before the window scales it

Super-sampling in paraLLEl-GS cannot hold 60 frames/s in Soulcalibur III's
battles on an M1 Pro, so the picture is shown without anti-aliasing. FXAA
3.11 (quality variant) smooths its polygon edges from the finished picture
at its own resolution, once per new picture. PS2_HOST_AA selects fxaa
(default) or off; the shader falls back to none if it does not compile.
